<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
                     xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <parent>
        <groupId>org.iromu.embabel.smith</groupId>
        <artifactId>embabel-smith-tools</artifactId>
        <version>0.1.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
    </parent>

    <artifactId>embabel-smith-tools-coding</artifactId>
    <name>embabel-smith-tools-coding</name>
    <description>
        The coding tool addon: the file and command surface a general coding agent needs,
        published as the two roles the runtime's own trust vocabulary already names — file
        (on by default) and shell (off until asked) — through an auto-configuration a host
        picks up by having this jar on its classpath. Every tool works inside one run root
        (smith.tools.coding.root, defaulting to the process working directory), and an
        escaping path is refused naming both path and root. Depends on the Embabel api and
        nothing of this repo's: not the runtime, not the studio, not the builder, and — as
        the inherited enforcer ban enforces — no poc-* artifact, though the command tool is
        the poc-7 bash tool extracted rather than depended on.
    </description>

    <dependencies>
        <!-- The platform's own tool interfaces (FileReadTools, FileWriteTools,
             PatternSearch), its ToolGroup factories, and Tool — the addon publishes
             upstream instances and authors three tools of its own against them. Declared
             rather than the starter: an addon publishes beans, it does not boot a platform,
             so the platform auto-configurations (and with them the model providers and the
             MCP-backed groups) stay off this classpath. This jar brings spring-boot-starter
             itself, which is where @AutoConfiguration and @ConditionalOnProperty come from. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>com.embabel.agent</groupId>
            <artifactId>embabel-agent-api</artifactId>
        </dependency>

        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.junit.jupiter</groupId>
            <artifactId>junit-jupiter</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.assertj</groupId>
            <artifactId>assertj-core</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-test</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>
</project>
